#: screen_tutorials/1
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Grand Piano"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/4
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "A concert grand piano typically measures 9 feet in length. A baby grand is 5 feet in length and can actually fit in a home."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/7
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Stove"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/10
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "A 'stove' refers to the oven plus the cooktop. A 'range' is the same as a 'stove', but helps distinguish between things that are called stoves but aren't in the kitchen, like wood-burning stoves."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/13
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Chair"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/16
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "A chair is a piece of furniture designed for one person to sit on. If it fits multiple people, it is technically not a chair."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/19
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Coffeepot"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/22
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "A coffee 'bean' is actually a seed of the coffee cherry - you can plant a coffee bean and grow a whole new shrub."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/25
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Magnifying Glass"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/28
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "A magnifying glass is actually the simplest form of a basic microscope. Historians believe a scientist named Alhazen created the first in 1021."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/31
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Window"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/34
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "A window sill is only located on the outside of a home. Inside, it is called a 'stool'."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/37
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Couch"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/40
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "According to Feng Shui principles, it is best to place a living room couch southwards, to optimize more light and within view of an entrance to provide security. A couch should never be placed in front of a window, as it can bring in chaotic energy."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/43
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Refrigerator"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/46
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "Around 20% of electricity in a home is used solely by the refrigerator at an average cost of $240 per year."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/49
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Bathtub"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/52
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "At the equator, bathtub water drains straight down."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/55
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Air fryer"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/58
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "Avoid using non-stick sprays in air fryers and only use oils, or cooking sprays. Non-stick sprays contain chemicals that can chip the coating."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/61
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Towels"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/64
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "Before terrycloth (the fluffy weaving style used in modern towels) was popularized, plain linens were used to dry off after baths."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/67
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Computer"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/70
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "Before the 1940’s the word \"computer\" was used to refer to a position where somebody had to calculate something very quickly."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/73
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Record Player"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/76
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "Black PVC pellets are used to create vinyl records, giving them their signature licorice look. Other colors decrease durability and collect dust more easily"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/79
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Bobby Pin"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/82
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "Bobby Pins are named after the popular 'bob cut', although they were almost named after their creator: Luis Marcus."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/85
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Cabinet"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/88
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "Cabinets apparently only refer to standalone decorative pieces that are not attached to any walls or other structures. Which means, there are no cabinets in this game, only cupboards."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/91
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Candelabra"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/94
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "Candle snuffers reduce the risk of accidental fires caused by blowing candles out, as well as help make you feel very cool."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/97
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Art"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/100
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "Caroline Shawk Brooks 1876 masterpiece, <i>Dreaming Iolanthe</i>, brought interest to the world in butter sculpting as an art form."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/103
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Dryer"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/106
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "Clothes dryers don't only dry clothes, but also kill pests such as bed bugs, ticks, and dust mites."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/109
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Fold-out Ironing Board"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/112
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "Clothes irons can also be used to remove chewing gum from garments, make paninis, and soften dents in tables."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/115
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Dishware"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/118
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "Combination utensils include: spork, knork, spifork, sporf, spife, and forkchops."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/121
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Detergent"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/124
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "Detergents can be defined as 'surfactants'. What 'surfactants' are unfortunately lie beyond the scope of this loading screen."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/127
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Money"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/130
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "Dollar bills are green because when they were created a color other than black was needed to make reproduction difficult, and green was seen as a color signifying stability."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/133
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Wall"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/136
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "Drywall means that there is no plumbing attached to a wall, as opposed to a wet wall- where there is plumbing connected."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/139
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Dust Bunny"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/142
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "Dust bunnies are held together by fibrous entanglement and static electricity."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/145
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Darkness"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/148
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "Eratosthenes used a stick and its small shadow to measure the circumference of the earth around 240 BCE."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/151
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Trash Can"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/154
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "Eugène Poubelle decreed in 1884 that landlords must provide three wastebins for residents to sort into compost, paper and cloth, and crockery and shells. To this day in France the word for trash can is 'la poubelle'."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/157
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Clock"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/160
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "The first clocks did not use hands or dials, but instead used bells. The word \"clock\" most likely comes from either the french word \"cloche\" or the german word \"glocke\", both meaning bell."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/163
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Dirty Laundry"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/166
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "GINETEX, formed in France in 1963, created the worldwide symbols for laundry care printed on every garment tag. Their guidelines are updated every five years."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/169
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Sink"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/172
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "Hot water valves are always on the left because readily available hot water was introduced second, and most people are right-handed."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/175
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Safe"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/178
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "If you have unlimited time, no safe is unbreakable."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/181
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Vacuum Cleaner"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/184
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "It is inadvisable to vacuum fireplace ash as the ash might be scattered further due to its small size. If there is a need however, simply cover the ash with wet coffee grounds to absorb the fine particulates."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/187
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Smoke Alarm"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/190
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "It is recommended to test smoke alarms monthly, and replace them after 10 years of use."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/193
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Literature"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/196
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "Literature is considered anything that has ever been written, including novels, cereal boxes, and this sentence."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/199
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Teddy Bear"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/202
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "Margarette Steiff created the first mass-produced stuffed animal in 1880 - a felt elephant intended for use as a pin cushion."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/205
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Microwave"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/208
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "Microwaves can microwave glass, paper, and most ceramics, but not metal."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/211
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Mirror"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/214
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "Mirrors reflect not only light, but sound too."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/217
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Holidays"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/220
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "Nepal has the highest number of nationally recognized public holidays, with 35. However, it also has a 6-day work week."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/223
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Door"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/226
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "Of the 17 doors in this game, only hinged and sliding doors are represented. Not shown: rotating, folding, and garage (up-and-over). The developers deeply regret this omission."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/229
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Desk"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/232
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "One crucial difference between desks and tables is that desks are largely designed to be used from only one side."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/235
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Shelf"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/238
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "One great way to secure your shelves from earthquakes: bungee cords."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/241
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Water Heater"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/244
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "Pilot lights unfortunately use roughly half of a heating system's total energy usage merely by staying lit. However, they can still be used during an electrical outage."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/247
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Toilet"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/250
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "Porcelain is used for toilets because it is waterproof, non-porous, and able to support weight."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/253
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Rat Trap"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/256
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "Regardless of what cartoons would have us believe, cheese is not as effective at trapping mice as peanut butter."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/259
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Dateviators"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/262
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "Rose-colored glasses have been used to help sufferers of migraines, to treat depression for Civil War veterans, and for chickens to prevent cannibalism."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/265
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Curtain Rod"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/268
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "Samuel Scottron was an African-American inventor who not only invented the curtain rod, but an adjustable mirror for cutting hair, the window cornice, and the leather hand strap used for riding on trolley cars."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/271
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Mysterious Objects"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/274
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "Sex toys are classified as 'novelties' in the United States to avoid the more stringent requirements and ingredient specifications of 'medical devices'."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/277
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Beauty Supplies"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/280
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "Some of the first makeup was eyeshadow invented by the Egyptians by grinding Lapis into a powder. The blue powder was only used by royalties and only seen by high ranking officials or other royals- hence the name \"royal blue\""
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/283
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Rejection"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/286
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "Susie Orbach conjectures that dating breakups are possibly more impactful than divorce because nonmarital relationships are not as socially recognized or defined."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/289
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Sporting Goods"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/292
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "The 'shuttle' in 'shuttlecock' refers to the back-and-forth motion of badminton like a loom. The 'cock' refers to the resemblance to feathers on a chicken."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/295
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "The Developers (Creators)"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/298
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "The 33 developers in this game volunteered to be featured. Brave souls."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/301
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Beverage"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/304
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "The alcohol in alcoholic beverages is ethanol."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/307
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Junk Drawer"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/310
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "The average drawer can hold around 50lbs of junk."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/313
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Box"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/316
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "The circular stamp printed on the outside of cardboard boxes is the Box Maker's Certificate - it tells interesting properties about the box itself such as its Bursting Test Score, Maximum Allowable Weight, and place of manufacture."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/319
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "D20"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/322
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "The d20's shape provides an equal five percent probability for each outcome, which is easier to calculate than the more common six-sided die."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/325
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Diary"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/328
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "The difference between a diary and a journal is that journals are made with the intention of somebody to read them. Diaries are not."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/331
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Electricity"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/334
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "The electrical activity in a typical human brain is enough to power a low-wattage bulb, like the one in the back of a refrigerator."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/337
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "HVAC"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/340
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "The first air conditioners were 7ft high, 6ft wide, and 20ft long."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/343
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Food"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/346
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "The first critiques of restaurants can be attributed to Alexandre Balthazar Laurent Grimod de La Reynière, who wrote eight volumes of criticism of the Paris cuisine scene from 1803-1812. He was accused of accepting bribes in exchange for positive reviews."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/349
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Lamp"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/352
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "The first lamps were used in prehistoric times and were made from seashells, animal fat, and bushes as the wicks."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/355
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Rubber Ducky"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/358
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "The first rubber ducks were made from solid rubber, and thus did not float. They were used as chew toys for children."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/361
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Office Supplies"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/364
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "The first stapler was created for King Louis XV who preferred it over wax seals. This model delivered gold staples and could only hold one at a time."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/367
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Time Capsule"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/370
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "The first Time Capsule started at the World's fair in 1938 and is scheduled to be open in 6939."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/373
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Crosstrainer"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/376
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "The first treadmill was invented in England in 1818 as a torture device for prisoners."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/379
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Trophy"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/382
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "The first trophies were made of the armor, weapons, and body parts of defeated enemies in warfare. Today they are largely made of plastic."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/385
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Bug in the Game"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/388
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "The first true computer bug was found in 1947, when an actual moth flew into the inner workings of the Mark II computer at Harvard."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/391
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "U.I."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/394
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "The first User Interface was created in 1962. Called \"Sketchpad\", users could draw, move, rotate, copy, and change the size of lines drawn directly on a screen."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/397
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Washer"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/400
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "The first washing machine was produced by Maytag and was called \"The hired girl.\""
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/403
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Floor"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/406
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "The floor, in addition to holding air conditioning, electrical wiring, plumbing, fire protection, and the like, also holds the ceiling of the storey beneath it."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/409
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Globe"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/412
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "The largest globe in the world is <i>Eartha</i> located in Yarmouth, Maine, former headquarters of a mapping company. Its diameter is 41 feet."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/415
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Overwhelming Sense of Existential Dread"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/418
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "The meaning of life has eluded scholars for millennia and caused countless existential dilemmas. Fortunately, it is now clear that the truth is simple: Date Everything."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/421
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Hangers"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/424
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "The modern clothes hanger was conceived in 1903 by Albert J. Parkhouse as an improvement over the coat-rack hook."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/427
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Anime Figurine"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/430
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "The most expensive anime figurine is the Gold Gunpla Kit - made of solid gold and worth over $200,000 each."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/433
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Toolbox"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/436
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "The most important tool in a toolbox is knowledge."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/439
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Video Game Console"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/442
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "The most memorable, rewarding, and highest paid part of game development is writing loading screen trivia."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/445
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Musical Triangle"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/448
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "The musical triangle is the only percussion instrument which can be struck on both an upstroke and downstroke."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/451
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Work"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/454
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "The oldest profession in the world is most likely either hunter, or toolmaker, though customer service as a profession began around the 1760s."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/457
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Shower"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/460
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "The philosopher Ibh Khaldun wrote in 1377 of people enjoying the sound of their voices singing while bathing."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/463
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Ship-in-a-Bottle"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/466
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
msgid "The practice of making ships in a bottle was started by sailors on large journeys who would make models of their ships in their free time."
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/469
msgctxt "Tag Titre écran de chargement"
msgid "Fan"
msgstr ""

#: screen_tutorials/472
msgctxt "Tag Anecdote écran de chargement"
